  "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_primate_comparison",
  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Comparing Black People to Primates",
  "description": "The meme's comparison of humans and gorillas, especially with the text 'after 3 million years of evolution', implicitly references a long-standing and deeply harmful racial stereotype that equates Black people with primates. This stereotype is used to demean and dehumanize Black individuals, suggesting they are less evolved, less intelligent, or more animalistic. The meme, by drawing this parallel, risks reinforcing this offensive trope, even if not explicitly targeting a specific race, by equating human leisure with primate behavior in a way that can be interpreted as demeaning to humans and perpetuating biological determinism.",
